module core part diagnostics

/**
Write a formatted diagnostic line to the process's standard output.

In a value function or a node's handler the line is written and flushed
where the call is executed. The text has a newline and goes to the
process stream, outside the run's record. The format string follows
`format`'s rules for value code, including `{wall_time}` and a marked place
whose argument is a `Marked`.

Type Args:
    As: The types of the positional arguments.
    Ks: The types of the arguments under their source names.

Args:
    fmt_str: The constant format string.
    args: The values that fill positional places, in argument order.
    kwargs: The values that fill places of the same names.

Raises:
    - `format.syntax`: a brace belongs to no place.
    - `format.argument`: a place has no argument, or asks for `{engine_time}`.
    - `format.unused`: no place takes an argument.
    - `format.specifier`: the argument does not admit a specifier or mark.

Examples:
    ~~~hgl
    debug_print("quote {:.2f} at {venue}", 101.25, venue: "test")
    ~~~

Notes:
    See the [formatting reference](https://github.com/hhenson/hgl_core/blob/main/spec/formatting.md#reference).

Rules:
    DBG-1, DBG-3, DBG-9, FMT-1, FMT-2, FMT-3, FMT-9
*/
export operator debug_print<...As, ...Ks>(
    const fmt_str: str, args: ...As, kwargs: ...{Ks})

/**
Write the line at the point of execution in a value function or handler.

Examples:
    ~~~hgl
    debug_print("{*}", Marked<i64>(value: 7, ticked: true))
    ~~~

Rules:
    DBG-1, DBG-3, DBG-9, FMT-9, OUT-2
*/
impl const fn debug_print<...As, ...Ks>(
    const fmt_str: str, args: ...As, kwargs: ...{Ks})
{
    write(format(fmt_str, ...args, ...kwargs) + "\n", flush: true)
}
